{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TaskPriority"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The executor determines how priority information affects the way tasks are scheduled."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The behavior varies depending on the executor currently being used."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Typically, executors attempt to run tasks with a higher priority"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before tasks with a lower priority."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"However, the semantics of how priority is treated are left up to each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"platform and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Executor"},{"type":"text","text":" implementation."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Child tasks automatically inherit their parent task’s priority."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Detached tasks created by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"detach(priority:operation:)"},{"type":"text","text":" don’t inherit task priority"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"because they aren’t attached to the current task."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In some situations the priority of a task is elevated —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that is, the task is treated as it if had a higher priority,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"without actually changing the priority of the task:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If a task runs on behalf of an actor,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a new higher-priority task is enqueued to the actor,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"then the actor’s current task is temporarily elevated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the priority of the enqueued task."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"This priority elevation allows the new task"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to be processed at the priority it was enqueued with."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If a higher-priority task calls the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"get()"},{"type":"text","text":" method,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"then the priority of this task increases until the task completes."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In both cases, priority elevation helps you prevent a low-priority task"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from blocking the execution of a high priority task,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which is also known as "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"priority inversion"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Comparable","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Copyable","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/CustomStringConvertible","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Decodable","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Encodable","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Equatable","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Escapable","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/RawRepresentable","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Sendable","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/SendableMetatype"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metad